## Why This Is Asked
In production, data distributions shift during events; online adaptation with tight latency is essential for edge-scale detectors. This tests practical drift handling and monitoring under real constraints.

## Key Concepts
- Online learning with bounded memory
- Concept drift detection (ADWIN, EDDM)
- Catastrophic forgetting mitigation (replay buffers, ensembles)
- Online calibration (isotonic regression, Platt scaling)
- Streaming infra and latency targets

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode: online drift detector usage
let detector = new ADWIN(0.002);
let model = new OnlineModel();
function onInstance(x, y){
  let pred = model.predict(x);
  detector.update(Math.abs(pred - y));
  if (detector.driftDetected()){
     model.updateWithReplayBuffer();
  }
  model.partialFit(x, y);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you compare drift detectors under varying stream rates?
- What metrics would you surface in production dashboards to detect degradation quickly?

